Hurricane Florence is making landfall  after thrashing the Carolinas all night  long with devastating flooding and  damaging winds forecasters are warning  that Florence's storm surge is  life-threatening and will be even worse  at high tide later this morning the  center of Florence is near Wilmington  North Carolina with maximum sustained  winds of 90 miles an hour that makes it  a category one but doesn't but don't  underestimate the power of this storm  rising water has flooded several coastal  cities swamp and businesses there are  reports of around 150 people still  needing rescue in New Bern North  Carolina more than 320 thousand homes  and businesses across the region have  lost power we have a team of  correspondents covering the storm CBS  Evening News anchor Jeff Glor leads our  coverage from Wilmington North Carolina  Florence began to bring its full force  to North Carolina overnight  lashing the coast was stinging rain  forceful wind and flooding in Belhaven a  rising river nearly swallowed the first  floor of this house as waves crashed  against its windows the lights were on  it is not clear if anyone was home one  of the hardest hit areas so far is  Newburgh where this morning around 150  people awaited rescue after more than 10  feet of powerful storm surge flooded the  town earlier as the storm slowly churned  toward Shore people who chose not to  evacuate got caught in floodwaters they  tried desperately to return to their  homes as the Neuse River overflowed  video taken Thursday night shows the  damage from wind gusts topping 100 miles  an hour they were strong enough to tear  the roofs and facades off stores and  destroy gas stations  in Moorhead City all that's left of this  building is a pile of crumbled wood much  of the wind damage was done even before  the storm surge there poured into the  streets this school in Jacksonville  suffered significant damage inside as  the panel's tore from the ceiling and  water rained down inside classrooms and  in Wilmington hurricane-force winds blew  transformers putting much of the city in  darkness
 

